# Cursor rules — Orders Desktop (WPF, .NET 10, C# 14)

- MVVM without third-party frameworks. ViewModels: ObservableObject + RelayCommand (ViewModels/Mvvm.cs). No logic in code-behind.
- Layers: Domain (no deps) <- Application (services, interfaces) <- Wpf; Infrastructure implements Application interfaces. Dependencies point inward.
- DI via Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting, host built in App.xaml.cs. Constructor injection only; no service locator.
- decimal for money, DateTimeOffset for time, inject IClock (never DateTime.Now in business logic).
- System.Text.Json only; cache JsonSerializerOptions. CultureInfo.InvariantCulture for machine data.
- Async: *Async suffix, CancellationToken, no async void (except WPF event handlers), no .Result/.Wait().
- Never swallow exceptions; ILogger<T> with structured placeholders. Never hardcode secrets.
- XAML: FlowDirection="RightToLeft", Hebrew labels, styles/brushes from Themes/*.xaml via StaticResource, standard WPF controls only, loading/empty/error states, AutomationProperties.Name.
- Tests: xUnit, Method_Scenario_Expected, tests before implementation.
- Before finishing: dotnet build, dotnet test, dotnet format --verify-no-changes. Ask before adding NuGet packages.
